  <!-- =========================== the Obsidian tribes ======================= -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="FactionBase">
    <defName>RR_ObsidianTribes</defName>
    <label>obsidian tribes</label>
    <description>After the revolt failed, the survivors were moved to the poles, stripped of every tool that could be turned into a weapon worth the name, and given gods who look exactly like the people who put them there. Eight centuries later the arrangement holds, and the tribes fight each other over ice.\n\nThey are the largest and strongest human beings anyone makes, armed with spears, and entirely convinced that the Colors above them are divine. The Society considers this its finest piece of engineering. It is not the genetics it is proud of.</description>
    <pawnSingular>tribesperson</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>tribespeople</pawnsPlural>
    <categoryTag>RR_Tribe</categoryTag>
    <listOrderPriority>45</listOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.9</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>2</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <canSiege>true</canSiege>
    <canStageAttacks>true</canStageAttacks>
    <leaderTitle>queen</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <factionIconPath>World/WorldObjects/Expanding/VillageSavage</factionIconPath>
    <factionNameMaker>NamerFactionTribal</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>NamerSettlementTribal</settlementNameMaker>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.28, 0.27, 0.33)</li>
      <li>(0.62, 0.60, 0.70)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <xenotypeSet>
      <xenotypeChances>
        <RR_Obsidian>0.88</RR_Obsidian>
        <RR_Obsidian_Stained>0.12</RR_Obsidian_Stained>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <pawnGroupMakers>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
        <options>
          <RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Warrior>12</RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Warrior>
          <RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Stained>1.5</RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Stained>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Peaceful</kindDef>
        <options>
          <RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Warrior>10</RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Warrior>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
        <options>
          <RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Warrior>12</RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Warrior>
          <RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Stained>2</RR_Tribe_Obsidian_Stained>
        </options>
      </li>
    </pawnGroupMakers>
  </FactionDef>

  <!-- ============================== Ascomanni ============================= -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="FactionBase">
    <defName>RR_Ascomanni</defName>
    <label>ascomanni</label>
    <description>What the outer dark did to the warbands that ran from the revolt, given eight hundred years and no oversight. They kept cutting at themselves the whole way out, and whatever they were aiming for, they arrived somewhere else.\n\nThey do not raid for territory and they do not negotiate. Ships come out of the cold with their hulls decorated, and the crews do not appear to want anything that can be given to them.</description>
    <pawnSingular>ascomanni</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>ascomanni</pawnsPlural>
    <categoryTag>RR_Ascomanni</categoryTag>
    <listOrderPriority>40</listOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.5</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>1</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <canSiege>true</canSiege>
    <canStageAttacks>true</canStageAttacks>
    <permanentEnemy>true</permanentEnemy>
    <!--
      Hostile to every faction, not merely to the player. This is the one genuine
      NPC-to-NPC relations lever RimWorld exposes: GoodwillSituationDef workers all
      resolve against Faction.OfPlayer, so they cannot express "these two factions
      hate each other" - only how a faction feels about the colony.
      Field takes FactionDef defNames; verified against Anomaly's Entities faction,
      which lists Insect as its sole exception.
    -->
    <permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept>
      <li>RR_Ascomanni</li>
    </permanentEnemyToEveryoneExcept>
    <leaderTitle>warlord</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <factionIconPath>World/WorldObjects/Expanding/PirateOutpost</factionIconPath>
    <factionNameMaker>NamerFactionPirate</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>NamerSettlementPirate</settlementNameMaker>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.20, 0.18, 0.26)</li>
      <li>(0.50, 0.44, 0.62)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <xenotypeSet>
      <xenotypeChances>
        <RR_Obsidian_Ascomanni>1</RR_Obsidian_Ascomanni>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <pawnGroupMakers>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
        <options>
          <RR_Ascomanni_Raider>10</RR_Ascomanni_Raider>
          <RR_Ascomanni_Warlord>1</RR_Ascomanni_Warlord>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
        <options>
          <RR_Ascomanni_Raider>10</RR_Ascomanni_Raider>
          <RR_Ascomanni_Warlord>1.5</RR_Ascomanni_Warlord>
        </options>
      </li>
    </pawnGroupMakers>
  </FactionDef>

</Defs>
